    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24846" root="صم" body-key="S">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صِمَّةٌ</span></b>  <i>Courageous;</i> (S, M, Msb, K;) applied to
a man; (S, M;) one <i>who renders deaf him
whom he smites.</i> (Er-Rághib, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also
the next preceding paragraph, in three places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
Also <i>A male serpent:</i> (S, K:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صِمَمٌ</span>. (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4- 
And <i>A female hedge-hog.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَمَامٌ</span>.

